+## When to Use
+
+- **Building any AI-powered feature** that OpenRouter supports — chatbots, coding assistants, agents, RAG pipelines, embeddings
+- **Comparing models by cost, latency, or capability** — use the models API to get real-time pricing and performance data
+- **Setting up model routing, fallbacks, or provider redundancy** — OpenRouter's auto router, fallbacks, and provider selection
+- **Implementing structured outputs or tool calling** — OpenRouter's response healing and JSON schema enforcement
+- **Working with multimodal inputs** — image, PDF, audio, and video across multiple models
+- **Managing API keys, workspaces, guardrails, or usage accounting** — OpenRouter's administration features
+- **Integrating with SDKs** — `@openrouter/sdk`, `@openrouter/agent`, OpenAI SDK (base URL override), Vercel AI SDK, LangChain, PydanticAI
+
+## Not For
+
+- **Questions about specific models' internals** (training data, architecture, fine-tuning details) → check the model provider's own docs, not OpenRouter
+- **On-premise or self-hosted model deployment** — OpenRouter is a cloud routing service, not a deployment platform → use Ollama, vLLM, or TGI
+- **Low-level networking or infrastructure** (load balancers, ingress controllers) — OpenRouter handles the infrastructure
+- **Custom model training or fine-tuning** — OpenRouter does not offer training APIs; use Hugging Face, Axolotl, or Unsloth
+- **Non-OpenRouter hosting** (AWS Bedrock, GCP Vertex AI) — those are separate platforms with their own APIs and docs
+- **Questions about closed beta features not yet in public docs** — check the docs index first; if it is not there, it is not ready for production use
+
+Load this skill when the user:
+- Explicitly mentions OpenRouter, `@openrouter`, or OpenRouter SDKs
+- Asks to build any AI-powered feature that OpenRouter supports
+- References model routing, variants, server tools, tool calling, structured outputs, embeddings, multimodal, observability, or API administration
+
+**Scope covers**:
+- chatbots, assistants, autonomous agents, coding agents
