+### D. SDK Decision Framework
+
+| Use Case | Recommended SDK | Rationale |
+|----------|-----------------|-----------|
+| Direct API access, custom orchestration | `@openrouter/sdk` (TS), Python SDK, Go SDK | Typed access to full OpenRouter API, low-level control |
+| **Agent loops, tools, stop conditions, state persistence** | `@openrouter/agent` (TS) | Built for multi-turn agents with tool execution, approval gates, context injection (`nextTurnParams`) |
+| Drop-in OpenAI replacement | OpenAI SDK with base URL override | Uses OpenRouter’s OpenAI-compatible endpoint (`/openai`) |
+| Vercel AI SDK | `@vercel/ai` + OpenRouter endpoint | Stream with OpenRouter backend |
+| LangChain integration | LangChain OpenRouter wrapper | Seamless integration with existing chains |
+| Anthropic Agent SDK | `@anthropic/ai` + OpenRouter via MCP | Use MCP server to connect to OpenRouter |
+
+**Rules**:
+- Do not default to `@openrouter/agent`. Use it only when multi-turn logic, tools, or state are needed.
+- The Agent SDK is TypeScript-first. Prefer TS examples unless user specifies otherwise.
+- For direct calls or embeddings, use Inference SDK or REST/OpenAI API.
+- Always link to current SDK docs from `llms.txt`, never guess paths.
